    "body": "Escalated effort:high to effort:max. Claim released.\n\nThe endpoint pin fails on unchanged upstream/main 31f8d03d. Run cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_g76_sources every_pass_runs_to_the_posted_end_z_inside_the_root_pass -- --exact. The 0.4 mm pass ends at Z8.416453640441397. G76 programs Z8.\n\nA safe extension needs partial-turn helical arcs. Fanuc and Tormach threadHalfTurn currently require antipodal endpoints and derive lead as twice the axial travel. The threading verifier in crates/motion/src/turning/thread_law.rs identifies meridian crossings by arc parity. Changing only the last axial endpoint changes the lead. Generalizing those contracts needs coordinated geometry, posting and verifier work.\n\nThe held failing pin and scope decision are pushed at mkinney:issue/1896-thread-pass-ends, commit 145dcc86. No production code changed. No draft PR was opened. The quick gate, clippy and mutations were not run because no fix was implemented. No goldens changed.\n\nThe inherited sccache wrapper could not create its cache directory under the sandbox. Unsetting RUSTC_WRAPPER allowed the pin to run. No approval was requested.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
